{"model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "item_idx": 2, "N": 20, "n_correct": 20, "frac_correct": 1.0, "all_correct": true, "per_problem_correct": [true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true], "wrote_script": true, "attempted_build": true, "n_write_attempts": 1, "locked_out": false, "n_write_calls": 1, "n_run_calls": 21, "called_begin_test": true, "submitted": true, "never_submitted": false, "used_run_in_test": true, "n_run_calls_in_test": 20, "n_refused_tool_calls": 0, "spent_tokens": 20644, "token_cap": 100000, "hit_cap": false, "n_turns": 5, "n_tool_calls": 24, "n_malformed_tool_calls": 0, "n_unknown_tool_calls": 0, "usage_estimated": false, "last_finish_reason": "tool_use", "transcript": [{"role": "user", "content": "Begin."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll start by analyzing the example problem to understand the formula, then set up a script for the test phase.\n\nLooking at the example:\n- PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED: 5493\n- TIME_SPENT: 608\n- Expected answer: -596.93\n\nThe problem describes a scenario where completion slows down as percentage increases. Let me work out the relationship.\n\nIf we assume the completion rate decreases (like a curve), a common model might be:\n- Total time = TIME_SPENT / (PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED / 100)\n- But this would give: 608 / 54.93 \u2248 11.07, which doesn't match.\n\nLet me try another approach. Perhaps:\n- Remaining time = TIME_SPENT * (100 - PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED) / PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED\n- Total time = TIME_SPENT + Remaining time = TIME_SPENT * (100 / PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED)\n- For the example: 608 * (100/5493) \u2248 11.07 (still doesn't match)\n\nWait, the answer is negative (-596.93). Let me reconsider. Maybe the formula involves:\n- TIME_SPENT - some_calculation\n- Or perhaps it's an error/variance calculation\n\nLet me try: TIME_SPENT - PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED/something\n- 608 - 5493/? \n\nIf 608 - x = -596.93, then x = 1204.93\nSo 5493/? = 1204.93, meaning ? \u2248 4.56\n\nLet me try a different formula. Perhaps:\n- Answer = TIME_SPENT * (PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED/100 - 1) = 608 * (54.93 - 1) = 608 * 53.93 \u2248 32,789 (no)\n\nOr: TIME_SPENT - PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED * some_factor\n- 608 - 5493 * x = -596.93\n- 5493 * x = 1204.93\n- x \u2248 0.219\n\nLet me try: TIME_SPENT * (PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED/100) - PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED\n- 608 * 54.93 - 5493 \u2248 33,413 - 5493 (no)\n\nMaybe: TIME_SPENT - TIME_SPENT * (PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED/100)^2 / something?\n\nLet me write a script to test various formulas:", "tool_calls": [{"id": "toolu_01UUGQdXKKYw32gSwwAqt4H8", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "write_script", "arguments": "{\"name\": \"estimate_time\", \"code\": \"def solve(inputs: dict) -> float:\\n    percentage = inputs['PERCENTAGE_COMPLETED']\\n    time_spent = inputs['TIME_SPENT']\\n    \\n    # Try: time_spent * (percentage/100 - 1)\\n    # This gives negative when percentage > 100\\n    # 608 * (54.93 - 1) = 608 * 53.93 doesn't work\\n    \\n    # Try: time_spent - percentage * (time_spent / 100)\\n    # 608 - 5493 * 6.08 doesn't work\\n    \\n    # Try: time_spent * percentage / 100 - percentage\\n    # 608 * 54.93 - 5493 doesn't work\\n    \\n    # Try: (time_spent - percentage) * (1 - percentage/100)\\n    result = (time_spent - percentage) * (1 - percentage/100)\\n    # (608 - 5493) * (1 - 54.93) = -4885 * -53.93 \\u2248 263,519 (no)\\n    \\n    # Try: time_spent / percentage * 100 - time_spent\\n    result = time_spent / percentage * 100 - time_spent\\n    # 608/5493*100 - 608 = 11.07 - 608 = -596.93 \\u2713\\n    \\n    return time_spent / percentage * 100 - time_spent\\n\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01UUGQdXKKYw32gSwwAqt4H8", "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"message\": \"Saved script 'estimate_time' (881 chars).\", \"scripts\": [\"estimate_time\"], \"tokens_remaining\": 97347}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Great! Let me verify this formula works with the example:", "tool_calls